1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,020
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 7)

3
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,920
Your bed is so comfortable.

4
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,999
I'm staying at your place tonight.

5
00:01:14,079 --> 00:01:15,640
I'll just crash here, okay?

6
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:30,880
You haven't even been drinking.

7
00:01:31,519 --> 00:01:32,519
Why are you blushing?

8
00:01:36,519 --> 00:01:37,519
You did this to me.

9
00:01:39,239 --> 00:01:40,840
When did I do anything to you?

10
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,599
You're the one messing with me, okay?

11
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:52,560
Let me ask you something.

12
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,920
Does what you said last time still count?

13
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,600
Huh? What was it?

14
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,239
You said if I won the lottery,

15
00:02:00,319 --> 00:02:01,719
you'd be my assistant.

16
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:05,519
Yeah, I did.

17
00:02:06,319 --> 00:02:08,120
I, Jiang Weibang, am a man of my word.

18
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,759
No way, did you actually win?

19
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:20,800
See for yourself.

20
00:02:21,639 --> 00:02:22,639
No way!

21
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,440
Damn, you really won!

22
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,119
What prize did you get?

23
00:02:25,199 --> 00:02:26,199
How much?

24
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,240
That's beside the point.

25
00:02:30,639 --> 00:02:32,040
The point is, are you in or not?

26
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,639
How is that beside the point?

27
00:02:33,719 --> 00:02:34,719
How much?

28
00:02:39,719 --> 00:02:41,159
If you take the job,

29
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,840
I'll split half of it with you.

30
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,119
Half?

31
00:02:47,199 --> 00:02:48,079
Yeah.

32
00:02:48,159 --> 00:02:49,799
Then of course I'm in,

33
00:02:49,879 --> 00:02:50,879
Boss Li.

34
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:55,359
Are you doing this for
me, or for the money?

35
00:02:55,439 --> 00:02:56,919
For the money, obviously!

36
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,295
I didn't even get a good look.

37
00:03:02,319 --> 00:03:03,160
You...

38
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,240
Classic you.

39
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,160
You can come work for me,

40
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,120
but you need to tone
down that temper of yours.

41
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,439
Tone down my temper?

42
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,280
I'm not saying you have a bad temper,

43
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:19,895
it's just that you always pick a fight
with Boss P'Eng whenever you meet.

44
00:03:19,919 --> 00:03:21,400
He's my future boss.

45
00:03:22,039 --> 00:03:23,719
It won't look good if you keep doing that.

46
00:03:24,759 --> 00:03:26,999
Well, he's the one who keeps
provoking me for no reason.

47
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,840
Can't you just do it for me?

48
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:32,319
And for the money?

49
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:34,439
Just hold back a little.

50
00:03:37,639 --> 00:03:39,160
So what you're saying is,

51
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,679
you want me to be like you

52
00:03:41,759 --> 00:03:42,840
and be a total pushover?

53
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:46,560
Me?

54
00:03:47,599 --> 00:03:48,639
A pushover?

55
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,559
I refuse to be a pushover.

56
00:03:52,639 --> 00:03:53,879
It's way too exhausting.

57
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,599
Everyday folks at the bottom like us

58
00:03:58,319 --> 00:04:00,479
have to be willing to
push back and flip the table

59
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,560
so people don't walk all over us.

60
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:05,880
If he doesn't even respect me

61
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:07,400
or care about my feelings,

62
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:09,639
why on earth should I care about his?

63
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:14,039
But have you ever thought that

64
00:04:14,919 --> 00:04:16,959
by always going head-to-head
with people like this,

65
00:04:17,319 --> 00:04:18,680
you might end up losing a lot?

66
00:04:21,639 --> 00:04:23,240
I'm not afraid of losing anything.

67
00:04:24,439 --> 00:04:27,119
Even a best friend I used to
spend every single day with

68
00:04:27,199 --> 00:04:28,839
could just up and leave without a word.

69
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,120
You're the one who taught me that, Milan.

70
00:04:34,759 --> 00:04:36,199
Still, I have to thank you

71
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,319
for making me realize

72
00:04:38,399 --> 00:04:40,199
that the only person
I can rely on is myself.

73
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:44,240
I didn't have a choice back then.

74
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:46,080
When I became a trainee,

75
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,016
the agency forbade me from
contacting anyone privately

76
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,679
and deleted all my contacts.

77
00:04:49,759 --> 00:04:50,439
There was nothing I could do.

78
00:04:50,519 --> 00:04:51,519
Alright,

79
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,160
let's drop it.

80
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,240
It's all in the past.

81
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,040
Don't worry,

82
00:05:08,279 --> 00:05:09,720
I'll be your assistant.

83
00:05:10,879 --> 00:05:12,160
After all,

84
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,960
it's not like I have another job right now.

85
00:05:32,319 --> 00:05:33,959
Why are you so nice to Pao Bei?

86
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:39,399
Because he's worth it.

87
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,120
What are you doing?

88
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:21,960
What?

89
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,160
Do you still not trust me?

90
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:26,240
Tell me what you're up to first.

91
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:38,120
Put this on first,

92
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:41,040
and I'll take you to the place
you're really curious about.

93
00:06:41,759 --> 00:06:43,120
Don't try anything funny.

94
00:06:43,639 --> 00:06:45,199
The kids are still downstairs.

95
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:46,576
I had Mingkun take care of everything.

96
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,600
Stop worrying.

97
00:07:09,279 --> 00:07:10,279
Where are we?

98
00:07:12,199 --> 00:07:14,159
Haven't you always been
curious about this place?

99
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,519
You even stole the key just to sneak in.

100
00:07:19,319 --> 00:07:22,160
So this is that mysterious room.

101
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,400
Well, you made it so secretive,

102
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,536
it naturally makes people want to know

103
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,760
what actually goes on in here.

104
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:30,000
So,

105
00:07:31,759 --> 00:07:33,799
were you afraid of people finding out

106
00:07:33,879 --> 00:07:35,720
because you wanted to hide your girly side?

107
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,720
Girly side?

108
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,800
More like childlike innocence.

109
00:08:01,959 --> 00:08:03,519
All of these

110
00:08:04,079 --> 00:08:07,279
are gifts my mom gave
me before she passed away.

111
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,240
I had no idea

112
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,959
he had such a quiet and gentle side.

113
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:30,360
Can I...

114
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,200
Can I ask you a question?

115
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:34,919
Go ahead.

116
00:08:37,879 --> 00:08:39,879
When did your mom...

117
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:42,080
When did she pass away?

118
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,840
Probably...

119
00:08:50,919 --> 00:08:52,720
Probably when I was around Xiaotong's age.

120
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,080
You must miss her a lot.

121
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:07,640
Don't look at me with
that pitying expression.

122
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,720
OK?

123
00:09:11,039 --> 00:09:12,200
I'm filthy rich.

124
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,176
You should worry about yourself instead.

125
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,200
Okay.

126
00:09:19,039 --> 00:09:20,199
By the way,

127
00:09:20,279 --> 00:09:21,816
there are snacks and drinks over there.

128
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:22,880
Want to go check them out?

129
00:09:24,559 --> 00:09:26,320
Give my stomach a break.

130
00:09:27,759 --> 00:09:29,279
I'm seriously stuffed.

131
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,240
Actually,

132
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,639
before I met you,

133
00:10:01,159 --> 00:10:02,200
I felt like I was

134
00:10:03,159 --> 00:10:05,440
just a heartless money-making machine.

135
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,760
But after meeting you,

136
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:09,919
it suddenly hit me—

137
00:10:10,919 --> 00:10:11,919
wow,

138
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,799
my life can actually be this exciting.

139
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,120
Someone actually dares to talk back to me,

140
00:10:18,759 --> 00:10:20,159
and even fight with me.

141
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:22,559
Do you have any idea

142
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,279
how much that makes me

143
00:10:27,879 --> 00:10:30,399
feel like an actual human being?

144
00:10:34,279 --> 00:10:35,279
Today,

145
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,879
hanging out with you guys all day

146
00:10:38,879 --> 00:10:40,720
and having a home-cooked meal together...

147
00:10:43,519 --> 00:10:44,679
I was genuinely happy.

148
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,120
Happy from the bottom of my heart.

149
00:10:50,679 --> 00:10:51,840
So,

150
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,360
you kept thanking me today,

151
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:57,600
but really,

152
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,720
the one who should be saying thank you

153
00:11:02,879 --> 00:11:03,919
is me.

154
00:11:09,759 --> 00:11:10,759
What's so funny?

155
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:14,080
I rarely open up like this, okay?

156
00:11:14,879 --> 00:11:16,159
Could you show a little respect?

157
00:11:22,039 --> 00:11:23,160
It's just that hearing you

158
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,800
suddenly talk like a normal human being

159
00:11:25,399 --> 00:11:27,919
is a little hard to get used to.

160
00:11:29,519 --> 00:11:30,519
A normal human being?

161
00:11:31,919 --> 00:11:32,919
Are you insulting me?

162
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,880
Then what was I speaking before?

163
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,480
Gibberish?

164
00:11:38,159 --> 00:11:39,360
Not at all!

165
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:41,480
Talking like a human
just means saying things

166
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,120
that make people feel

167
00:11:45,279 --> 00:11:46,879
strangely sympathetic

168
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,000
and weirdly touched.

169
00:11:52,679 --> 00:11:55,799
In my book, that's called
"human talk" for short.

170
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:59,679
Does that make sense to you?

171
00:12:02,799 --> 00:12:04,919
Stop being so sensitive, okay?

172
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:07,919
Sensitive?

173
00:12:09,399 --> 00:12:11,440
I think you're the sensitive one here.

174
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:12,679
Me?

175
00:12:12,759 --> 00:12:14,000
How am I sensitive?

176
00:12:14,879 --> 00:12:16,159
I am not sensitive at all, okay?

177
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,720
Not sensitive, huh?

178
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,480
Really not sensitive?

179
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:27,360
What are you doing?

180
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:30,720
Stop it, that tickles!

181
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,840
Can I ask you a question?

182
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,199
Yeah.

183
00:13:03,279 --> 00:13:04,279
Go ahead.

184
00:13:06,399 --> 00:13:07,399
Do you...

185
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,200
Do you like me?

186
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:19,559
Well, do you hate me?

187
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:23,399
Of course I don't hate you.

188
00:13:24,639 --> 00:13:25,759
Then that means you like me,

189
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:27,240
right?

190
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:39,799
I'm a little thirsty.

191
00:13:39,879 --> 00:13:40,919
I'm gonna go grab a drink.

192
00:14:03,039 --> 00:14:04,480
Don't dodge my question.

193
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,439
You do like me,

194
00:14:08,519 --> 00:14:09,519
don't you?

195
00:14:17,039 --> 00:14:18,480
I know you like me.

196
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,679
Look how red your ears are.

197
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,480
Let me cool them down for you.

198
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,440
What are you doing?

199
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,320
And you said you weren't sensitive.

200
00:14:37,399 --> 00:14:39,479
Just this much and you're
already weak in the knees.

201
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:41,840
So cute.

202
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,360
Even if you don't say it,

203
00:16:11,039 --> 00:16:12,039
your actions

204
00:16:12,799 --> 00:16:14,320
speak louder than words.

205
00:16:18,159 --> 00:16:19,320
I like you.

206
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,960
But I don't think we're
right for each other.

207
00:16:34,399 --> 00:16:35,879
Why aren't we right for each other?

208
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:38,319
I'm not done talking yet.

209
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:39,440
I just...

210
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,520
I'm not done yet.

211
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:51,639
I just...

212
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:57,600
I know what's holding you back.

213
00:16:59,039 --> 00:17:00,480
But I don't care about any of that.

214
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,319
All I care about

215
00:17:03,399 --> 00:17:04,839
is how I feel about you right now.

216
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:10,839
I want you.

217
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,279
I want to be with you.

218
00:17:17,519 --> 00:17:18,519
Right here,

219
00:17:19,559 --> 00:17:20,680
there is no boss,

220
00:17:21,759 --> 00:17:22,799
and no debtor.

221
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,680
There are just two men here,

222
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,279
named Pao Bei

223
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:34,359
and P'Eng.

224
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,359
Two people who love each other.

225
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,920
And that's enough.

226
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,640
Then,

227
00:17:56,559 --> 00:17:58,279
please let me be yours tonight.

228
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:14,880
Thank you.

229
00:21:35,319 --> 00:21:38,680
"Thank you for giving me a warm winter."

230
00:21:42,799 --> 00:21:44,519
This was sent from abroad.

231
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:46,320
Yeah.

232
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,400
From Norway.

233
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,480
Well, well.

234
00:21:54,519 --> 00:21:56,559
Boss P'Eng even has romantic flings abroad.

235
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:13,240
That's right.

236
00:22:14,359 --> 00:22:16,479
With your Boss P'Eng's looks

237
00:22:16,559 --> 00:22:17,800
and charm,

238
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,360
he's bound to be a hit

239
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:20,999
wherever he goes.

240
00:22:21,079 --> 00:22:22,079
Oh, really?

241
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,519
What are you doing?

242
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:51,560
Take a look.

243
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:53,200
Isn't the handwriting the same?

244
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:03,239
What do you mean?

245
00:23:03,319 --> 00:23:05,039
You wrote this yourself?

246
00:23:06,359 --> 00:23:07,239
Yeah.

247
00:23:07,319 --> 00:23:08,600
Silly boy.

248
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:09,880
I sent it to myself.

249
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:11,440
Get it now?

250
00:23:13,279 --> 00:23:15,160
So, the picture on this...

251
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,599
The snowy mountains are gorgeous.

252
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:54,400
Have you ever seen snow?

253
00:23:55,759 --> 00:23:56,759
No.

254
00:23:57,519 --> 00:23:59,319
It never snows here in Mancheng.

255
00:24:00,039 --> 00:24:01,640
I probably

256
00:24:01,720 --> 00:24:04,319
won't ever get the chance
to see snow in my life.

257
00:24:06,599 --> 00:24:09,079
Norway was where I saw
snow for the first time, too.

258
00:24:11,079 --> 00:24:12,400
The snow there has a kind of...

259
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:14,880
How do I put it?

260
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:17,640
It smells like Super Cedar.

261
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:18,839
It's a cologne.

262
00:24:20,079 --> 00:24:21,839
But I don't even wear cologne.

263
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Doesn't matter.

264
00:24:26,759 --> 00:24:29,160
Anyway, when the time comes,

265
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:29,920
once winter rolls around,

266
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,216
I'll take you to Norway to
see the snow, and you'll know.

267
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:33,240
Okay.

268
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:36,439
You know,

269
00:24:36,519 --> 00:24:39,599
in Norway, the sun
doesn't rise until 10 a.m.,

270
00:24:40,319 --> 00:24:42,559
and it sets at 1 p.m.

271
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:44,720
There are only three hours of daylight.

272
00:24:45,759 --> 00:24:48,080
Why is it so short?

273
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:49,160
I know, right?

274
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:51,840
So when I first got there,

275
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:53,240
I really couldn't get used to it.

276
00:24:54,079 --> 00:24:56,119
I always felt like my
time was being stolen.

277
00:24:58,200 --> 00:24:59,200
Later on,

278
00:25:00,599 --> 00:25:02,839
I realized there's plenty
to do at night, too.

279
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:07,680
I stopped stressing over having
only three hours of daylight.

280
00:25:10,559 --> 00:25:12,279
Slowly, I realized

281
00:25:12,359 --> 00:25:13,719
the night is actually pretty nice.

282
00:25:14,839 --> 00:25:17,519
The darkness brings me peace and calm.

283
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:23,440
Unlike the daytime,

284
00:25:24,279 --> 00:25:29,440
when I have to put on a fake persona.

285
00:25:35,799 --> 00:25:36,799
Look.

286
00:25:37,319 --> 00:25:38,919
The scenery there is truly breathtaking.

287
00:25:40,519 --> 00:25:42,160
Too bad. I really regret

288
00:25:42,759 --> 00:25:44,799
not taking the cable car
up the mountain back then.

289
00:25:48,279 --> 00:25:50,200
But if you were there,

290
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:52,039
I probably would've gone on it.

291
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:01,720
Well,

292
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:05,079
I hope I can save up enough
money to travel abroad.

293
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:08,400
Look.

294
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,479
Such a beautiful

295
00:26:10,559 --> 00:26:13,400
postcard from 69 degrees north latitude,

296
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:14,999
and I could only send it to myself.

297
00:26:15,079 --> 00:26:16,079
What a shame.

298
00:26:18,319 --> 00:26:20,839
Next time, if you're not with me,

299
00:26:22,799 --> 00:26:23,799
I think.

300
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:27,640
I'll send one to you.

301
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:34,079
People always say Norway is freezing.

302
00:26:36,640 --> 00:26:39,480
But when you actually go there,

303
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,000
bundle up in thick clothes,

304
00:26:43,759 --> 00:26:45,160
step onto that white snow,

305
00:26:47,279 --> 00:26:49,920
and watch your breath turn into white mist,

306
00:26:52,079 --> 00:26:53,079
you'll realize

307
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,000
that in fact,

308
00:26:56,680 --> 00:27:01,039
it's the warmest winter of all.

309
00:27:04,279 --> 00:27:05,279
That's why.

310
00:27:06,279 --> 00:27:07,640
I wrote that line.

311
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:13,680
Then,

312
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:16,319
give this one to me.

313
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:19,480
Let's pretend the
postcard you sent back then

314
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,839
has finally reached me now.

315
00:27:22,359 --> 00:27:23,359
Okay.

316
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:54,160
Pao Bei.

317
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:18,480
Pao Bei.

318
00:28:26,599 --> 00:28:27,599
Pao Bei.

319
00:28:32,559 --> 00:28:33,680
Pao Bei.

320
00:28:48,359 --> 00:28:49,359
Pao Bei.

321
00:29:16,799 --> 00:29:19,279
P'Eng, is that you?

322
00:29:19,359 --> 00:29:20,640
Mom?

323
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:21,880
Is that you?

324
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:23,480
P'Eng.

325
00:29:24,039 --> 00:29:25,039
It's Mom.

326
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:27,560
I'm right here.

327
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:28,640
Come here.

328
00:29:37,440 --> 00:29:38,720
Mom!

329
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:42,480
Mom!

330
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,240
How did you...

331
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:46,759
end up like this?

332
00:29:48,519 --> 00:29:50,000
You're finally here.

333
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:53,039
Didn't you see the hint I left for you?

334
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:55,640
The picture we painted together.

335
00:29:55,720 --> 00:29:57,279
Didn't you find it?

336
00:29:58,359 --> 00:30:00,200
That painting...

337
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:03,440
So you were the one who buried it?

338
00:30:06,920 --> 00:30:08,039
Don't take my child away!

339
00:30:08,839 --> 00:30:09,360
No!

340
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:09,679
Come here!

341
00:30:09,759 --> 00:30:10,640
No!

342
00:30:10,720 --> 00:30:11,080
Mom!

343
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:11,600
Stop!

344
00:30:11,680 --> 00:30:12,039
Mom!

345
00:30:12,119 --> 00:30:12,800
No!

346
00:30:12,880 --> 00:30:14,039
Don't take my child away!

347
00:32:02,119 --> 00:32:03,519
Good morning, Mr. Pao Bei.

348
00:32:06,519 --> 00:32:07,400
Good morning.

349
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:08,719
Did you sleep well?

350
00:32:08,799 --> 00:32:11,136
As Master P'Eng instructed, the
kids have been dropped off at school.

351
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:12,039
Now that you're awake,

352
00:32:12,119 --> 00:32:13,959
you may head to the
dining room for breakfast.

353
00:32:14,559 --> 00:32:16,000
I slept pretty well.

354
00:32:18,480 --> 00:32:19,039
Where...

355
00:32:19,119 --> 00:32:20,279
Where is he?

356
00:32:20,359 --> 00:32:22,439
Master P'Eng was in the
kitchen bright and early,

357
00:32:22,519 --> 00:32:24,439
making breakfast with Mr. A Pong.

358
00:32:24,519 --> 00:32:26,519
He's just waiting for you
to wake up and enjoy it.

359
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:28,160
He made breakfast himself?

360
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:36,959
What's this?

361
00:32:37,039 --> 00:32:38,279
Master P'Eng had this prepared.

362
00:32:38,319 --> 00:32:39,599
It's your outfit for today.

363
00:32:40,880 --> 00:32:42,880
Why do I have to dress so formally?

364
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:44,680
Are we going to some kind of event?

365
00:32:45,839 --> 00:32:46,999
I wouldn't know about that.

366
00:32:47,079 --> 00:32:49,640
But I'm sure you'll look dashing in it.

367
00:32:50,519 --> 00:32:52,320
Once you've washed up and gotten dressed,

368
00:32:52,400 --> 00:32:53,719
you can head downstairs.

369
00:32:53,799 --> 00:32:55,559
We'll be waiting for
you in the dining room.

370
00:33:06,720 --> 00:33:09,160
What on earth is this guy up to?

371
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:16,920
Good morning.

372
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:19,920
Whoa.

373
00:33:20,839 --> 00:33:22,800
Another huge breakfast spread today.

374
00:33:22,880 --> 00:33:24,120
Did you cook this yourself?

375
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:25,600
Yep.

376
00:33:25,680 --> 00:33:26,560
I made all of this.

377
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,400
What do you think?

378
00:33:27,480 --> 00:33:28,920
Come on, you made it?

379
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,216
All you did was toss the ingredients

380
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,616
I chopped and seasoned into the pan.

381
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:35,799
A joint effort between Tailan's most
handsome boss and its finest chef.

382
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:39,320
Where is he?

383
00:33:39,400 --> 00:33:40,080
Is he up yet?

384
00:33:40,160 --> 00:33:42,200
Mr. Pao Bei should be down any minute.

385
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:14,720
Are you...

386
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:17,479
heading to a fashion gala or something?

387
00:34:17,559 --> 00:34:19,720
Dressed to the nines
first thing in the morning.

388
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:21,439
You're so weird.

389
00:34:21,519 --> 00:34:22,960
Go ask him about it.

390
00:34:27,239 --> 00:34:29,999
Look at you, so dashing and debonair.

391
00:34:30,079 --> 00:34:32,719
Dressed like that, everyone
can tell you're mine.

392
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:34,999
Yours?

393
00:34:35,079 --> 00:34:36,720
Of course he's Boss P'Eng's.

394
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:38,599
Everyone here works for Boss P'Eng.

395
00:34:38,679 --> 00:34:39,679
Isn't that right?

396
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:41,640
Aren't you one of his people, too?

397
00:34:42,400 --> 00:34:44,320
He agreed to be my assistant last night.

398
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:45,959
So, technically,

399
00:34:46,039 --> 00:34:47,839
you're part of Boss
P'Eng's company now, too.

400
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:49,840
Just eat your congee.

401
00:34:51,320 --> 00:34:53,079
I made all of this specially for you.

402
00:34:53,159 --> 00:34:54,159
Mhm.

403
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,280
Why don't I get this kind of service?

404
00:34:57,880 --> 00:34:59,360
You want service like this?

405
00:35:00,960 --> 00:35:04,639
Then take good care of me
and your boss from now on.

406
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:07,480
As if I care.

407
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:09,479
Stop piling up my plate.

408
00:35:09,559 --> 00:35:10,760
I can't finish all of this.

409
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,000
Well,

410
00:35:14,039 --> 00:35:15,135
eat this shumai first, then.

411
00:35:15,159 --> 00:35:16,159
It's really good.

412
00:35:22,159 --> 00:35:23,159
Is it good?

413
00:35:26,239 --> 00:35:27,239
Delicious.

414
00:35:43,400 --> 00:35:44,760
Master, slow down.

415
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:46,936
Keep eating like that and
I'll lose track of your calories.

416
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,000
Don't bother counting.

417
00:35:48,840 --> 00:35:51,360
I got a massive workout last night.

418
00:35:54,119 --> 00:35:55,400
I need to eat up.

419
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,880
You guys don't need to wait on me.

420
00:36:08,519 --> 00:36:09,840
I can manage on my own.

421
00:36:10,679 --> 00:36:12,039
Have you had breakfast yet?

422
00:36:12,119 --> 00:36:14,039
We only eat after the
masters have finished.

423
00:36:14,119 --> 00:36:15,119
Those are the rules.

424
00:36:16,159 --> 00:36:19,119
There's way too much
food here for us to finish.

425
00:36:19,199 --> 00:36:20,319
It'd be a shame to waste it.

426
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:22,080
Come sit down and eat with us.

427
00:36:23,039 --> 00:36:25,800
We're not allowed to dine at
the same table as the masters.

428
00:36:29,960 --> 00:36:31,800
Who made the rule that
they can't eat with us?

429
00:36:33,159 --> 00:36:34,159
Beats me.

430
00:36:34,719 --> 00:36:36,719
Probably a tradition passed
down by our ancestors.

431
00:36:37,559 --> 00:36:38,079
Don't worry about it.

432
00:36:38,159 --> 00:36:38,959
Just eat your food.

433
00:36:39,039 --> 00:36:39,760
Go on, eat.

434
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:40,639
Mhm.

435
00:36:40,719 --> 00:36:42,159
They're all still on empty stomachs,

436
00:36:42,719 --> 00:36:43,639
just standing there watching me eat.

437
00:36:43,719 --> 00:36:45,199
I can't take a single bite like this.

438
00:36:54,119 --> 00:36:54,440
Fine.

439
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:56,639
I'll make a special exception today.

440
00:36:56,719 --> 00:36:57,719
I'm in a good mood.

441
00:36:58,480 --> 00:36:59,400
Everyone, sit down

442
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:00,119
and eat together.

443
00:37:00,199 --> 00:37:01,280
No leftovers allowed.

444
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:02,479
Got that?

445
00:37:02,559 --> 00:37:03,559
Yes.

446
00:37:06,159 --> 00:37:06,599
Go on.

447
00:37:06,679 --> 00:37:07,679
Take a seat over there.

448
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,840
Now this is a first.

449
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:19,559
They actually get to eat my cooking.

450
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:22,000
Ever since you showed up,

451
00:37:22,079 --> 00:37:24,039
unusual things have been
happening more and more.

452
00:37:28,079 --> 00:37:29,079
This is good.

453
00:38:14,960 --> 00:38:15,999
Mingkun.

454
00:38:16,079 --> 00:38:18,135
These clothes are too hot
and get in the way of my work.

455
00:38:18,159 --> 00:38:20,039
I should just change
back into my own clothes.

456
00:38:20,119 --> 00:38:22,559
I'm afraid you'll have to
run that by the Master first.

457
00:38:23,559 --> 00:38:25,359
I'm just more used to
how things were before.

458
00:38:25,760 --> 00:38:27,439
Why is he suddenly acting like this?

459
00:38:27,519 --> 00:38:28,679
I'm not used to it at all.

460
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:30,535
These are the Master's orders.

461
00:38:30,559 --> 00:38:32,400
Their sole job is to assist you.

462
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:36,519
How did it come to this?

463
00:38:37,239 --> 00:38:39,280
Because you belong to the Master now.

464
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:42,840
Since when do I belong to him?

465
00:38:45,280 --> 00:38:46,720
After what happened last night,

466
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:49,000
don't tell me you're going
to pretend nothing happened?

467
00:38:57,519 --> 00:38:58,519
What happened?

468
00:38:59,960 --> 00:39:01,240
It's just a little prick.

469
00:39:01,320 --> 00:39:02,200
Ambulance!

470
00:39:02,280 --> 00:39:02,920
Call an ambulance!

471
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:03,639
Hurry!

472
00:39:03,719 --> 00:39:04,599
Hey, come back!

473
00:39:04,679 --> 00:39:05,519
It's just a tiny cut.

474
00:39:05,599 --> 00:39:06,880
It's no big deal.

475
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:07,599
Master,

476
00:39:07,679 --> 00:39:09,439
just put this band-aid
on and it'll be fine.

477
00:39:11,199 --> 00:39:12,440
I'm fine, really.

478
00:39:12,960 --> 00:39:14,720
If you keep overreacting like this,

479
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:16,959
I'm seriously going to start ignoring you.

480
00:39:17,039 --> 00:39:17,920
This one is waterproof.

481
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:19,320
You can keep it on in the shower.

482
00:39:24,719 --> 00:39:25,360
Master P'Eng,

483
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:26,280
Mr. Pao Bei.

484
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:28,240
I have some things to attend to over there,

485
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:29,920
so I'll go take care of them now.

486
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,000
Mhm.

487
00:39:32,039 --> 00:39:32,800
How is it?

488
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:33,880
Does it still hurt?

489
00:39:35,159 --> 00:39:36,800
Oh, so now you care if I'm in pain?

490
00:39:36,880 --> 00:39:38,680
When I was crying out in pain last night...

491
00:39:38,760 --> 00:39:39,800
"It hurts, it hurts!"

492
00:39:39,880 --> 00:39:41,600
Why were you enjoying it so much back then?

493
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:45,400
Isn't that why I made you
breakfast first thing this morning

494
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:46,560
and had people wait on you?

495
00:39:47,199 --> 00:39:47,680
What's wrong?

496
00:39:47,760 --> 00:39:48,800
Not satisfied?

497
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:51,959
I'd rather you didn't do any of this.

498
00:39:52,039 --> 00:39:53,575
Having all these people
hovering around me...

499
00:39:53,599 --> 00:39:54,760
I'm not used to it.

500
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:58,000
What's the big deal?
You'll learn to get used to it.

501
00:39:56,440 --> 00:39:57,800
You'll get used to it soon enough.

502
00:40:03,199 --> 00:40:04,519
After all,

503
00:40:04,599 --> 00:40:05,800
since you're mine,

504
00:40:05,880 --> 00:40:07,495
you'll need to start keeping pace with me.

505
00:40:07,519 --> 00:40:08,519
Got it?

506
00:40:09,280 --> 00:40:10,360
Me?

507
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:11,920
Since when am I yours?

508
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:14,159
What do you mean?

509
00:40:17,000 --> 00:40:18,119
I mean, I...

510
00:40:18,199 --> 00:40:21,239
Aren't you mine now?

511
00:40:23,760 --> 00:40:25,320
I mean, I'm my own person.

512
00:40:25,400 --> 00:40:26,880
I don't belong to anyone.

513
00:40:29,079 --> 00:40:30,159
Then last night...

514
00:40:31,119 --> 00:40:32,239
What was that?

515
00:40:35,079 --> 00:40:38,199
Just two consenting adults
blowing off some steam.

516
00:40:41,039 --> 00:40:42,440
Are you playing me again?

517
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:44,959
I was just joking with you.

518
00:40:45,039 --> 00:40:46,639
Why are you getting so worked up?

519
00:40:46,719 --> 00:40:48,559
Are you freaking playing me again?!

520
00:40:48,639 --> 00:40:49,679
Why are you yelling again?

521
00:40:49,719 --> 00:40:51,359
Can't we just talk like civilized people?

522
00:40:53,039 --> 00:40:54,240
It's fine, A Pong.

523
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:55,599
We're just messing around.

524
00:40:55,679 --> 00:40:57,095
Who the hell is messing around with you?!

525
00:40:57,119 --> 00:40:59,015
I told you to talk nicely
and watch your damn mouth!

526
00:40:59,039 --> 00:40:59,800
Are you deaf?!

527
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:00,559
What's it to you?

528
00:41:00,639 --> 00:41:01,760
Get lost!

529
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:02,720
Boss P'Eng,

530
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:04,615
let's just talk it out. We're
all on the same side here.

531
00:41:04,639 --> 00:41:06,519
You're going to scare
Pao Bei acting like this.

532
00:41:07,599 --> 00:41:09,360
I'm asking you one last time.

533
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,159
Last night...

534
00:41:13,599 --> 00:41:14,959
What the hell was that between us?

535
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:19,559
What did you two do last night?

536
00:41:22,760 --> 00:41:23,959
Him and me...

537
00:41:24,039 --> 00:41:25,039
The two of us...

538
00:41:26,719 --> 00:41:27,800
slept together.

539
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:28,920
What?

540
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:31,800
You... What did you just say?

541
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:32,920
Are you deaf?

542
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,495
I said we slept together. We hooked up.

543
00:41:34,519 --> 00:41:35,519
Get it now?

544
00:41:38,679 --> 00:41:39,679
P'Eng!

545
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:43,239
Don't be rude to our guest.
